tics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Orl%C3%A9ans"}],"explanation74":"Relief of Orléans: 1429. Joan of Arc participates in the French victory."},{"id":"EXP77-1454","nodeId":"EXP77-1454","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q121","subject":"The Boston Tea Party belongs to the background of which revolution?","value":"American Revolution","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Tea_Party"}],"explanation74":"The 1773 protest against British tea policy intensified the dispute between Britain and its North American colonies."},{"id":"EXP77-1455","nodeId":"EXP77-1455","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Otto I's imperial coronation is associated with the development of which polity?","value":"Holy Roman Empire","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_I,_Holy_Roman_Emperor"}],"explanation74":"Otto I was crowned emperor in Rome in 962, a foundational date in the history of the Holy Roman Empire."},{"id":"EXP77-1456","nodeId":"EXP77-1456","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q126","subject":"The conquest of Granada ended the rule of which dynasty in Iberia?","value":"Nasrid","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Medieval","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War"}],"explanation74":"The Nasrid emirate of Granada was the last Muslim-ruled state in Iberia; it fell in 1492."},{"id":"EXP77-1457","nodeId":"EXP77-1457","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"The Treaty of Breda of 1667 ended a war principally between which maritime rivals?","value":"England and the Netherlands","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Breda_(1667)"}],"explanation74":"Breda settled the Second Anglo-Dutch War, a conflict driven partly by overseas trade and naval rivalry."},{"id":"EXP77-1458","nodeId":"EXP77-1458","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q079","subject":"Belgium's 1830 revolution sought independence from which kingdom?","value":"Netherlands","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgian_Revolution"}],"explanation74":"The southern provinces broke away from the United Kingdom of the Netherlands to form Belgium."},{"id":"EXP77-1459","nodeId":"EXP77-1459","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q607","subject":"The arrival of the First Fleet at Sydney Cove established a British colony on which continent?","value":"Australia","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"place geography","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Fleet"}],"explanation74":"The First Fleet reached Sydney Cove in 1788, marking the beginning of the British colony of New South Wales."},{"id":"EXP77-1460","nodeId":"EXP77-1460","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Alaric's army, which sacked Rome in 410, belonged to which people?","value":"Visigoths","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sack_of_Rome_(410)"}],"explanation74":"Alaric led the Visigoths. The later sack of Rome in 455 was carried out by the Vandals."},{"id":"EXP77-1461","nodeId":"EXP77-1461","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Thermidorian Reaction","value":"1794","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermidorian_Reaction"}],"explanation74":"Thermidorian Reaction: 1794. Fall of Robespierre."},{"id":"EXP77-1462","nodeId":"EXP77-1462","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q189","subject":"First Council of Constantinople","value":"381","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Council_of_Constantinople"}],"explanation74":"First Council of Constantinople: 381. Separate event from the edict of 380."},{"id":"EXP77-1463","nodeId":"EXP77-1463","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"The Treaty of Hubertusburg concluded the central European phase of which war?","value":"Seven Years' War","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Hubertusburg"}],"explanation74":"The 1763 treaty restored peace between Prussia, Austria and Saxony at the end of the Seven Years' War."},{"id":"EXP77-1464","nodeId":"EXP77-1464","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"The Royal Observatory at Greenwich was founded primarily to improve which practical activity?","value":"Navigation","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"term function","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Observatory,_Greenwich"}],"explanation74":"Founded in 1675, the observatory supported astronomical work intended to improve navigation at sea."},{"id":"EXP77-1465","nodeId":"EXP77-1465","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Francis I was captured at Pavia during which series of conflicts?","value":"Italian Wars","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pavia"}],"explanation74":"The 1525 battle was fought during the Italian Wars between French and Habsburg forces."},{"id":"EXP77-1466","nodeId":"EXP77-1466","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q494","subject":"Peace of Utrecht","value":"1713","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Utrecht"}],"explanation74":"Peace of Utrecht: 1713. Major settlement of the Spanish Succession war."},{"id":"EXP77-1467","nodeId":"EXP77-1467","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q189","subject":"Which trio participated in the First Partition of Poland?","value":"Russia, Prussia, Austria","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"matching","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partitions_of_Poland"}],"explanation74":"Russia, Prussia and Austria divided Polish territory in 1772."},{"id":"EXP77-1468","nodeId":"EXP77-1468","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q122","subject":"The battles of Legnica and Mohi marked the advance of which forces into central Europe?","value":"Mongols","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasion_of_Europe"}],"explanation74":"Mongol forces invaded Poland and Hungary in 1241 and won at Legnica and Mohi."},{"id":"EXP77-1469","nodeId":"EXP77-1469","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Mary I's marriage to Philip linked the English crown to which dynasty?","value":"Habsburg","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_I_of_England"}],"explanation74":"Philip, later Philip II of Spain, belonged to the Habsburg dynasty."},{"id":"EXP77-1470","nodeId":"EXP77-1470","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q517","subject":"Mary, Queen of Scots, was executed during the reign of which English monarch?","value":"Elizabeth I","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary,_Queen_of_Scots"}],"explanation74":"Mary Stuart was executed in England in 1587, during Elizabeth I's reign."},{"id":"EXP77-1471","nodeId":"EXP77-1471","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"The Treaty of the Pyrenees settled a conflict between which two monarchies?","value":"France and Spain","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_the_Pyrenees"}],"explanation74":"The 1659 treaty ended the Franco-Spanish War and confirmed French gains along the border."},{"id":"EXP77-1472","nodeId":"EXP77-1472","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"The Luddites are chiefly associated with resistance to which development?","value":"Mechanised textile production","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luddite"}],"explanation74":"Luddite protests targeted textile machinery and changes to labour conditions in early industrial Britain."},{"id":"EXP77-1473","nodeId":"EXP77-1473","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"The Christianisation of Kievan Rus' under Vladimir I drew primarily on which tradition?","value":"Byzantine Christianity","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianization_of_Kievan_Rus'"}],"explanation74":"Vladimir's adoption of Christianity connected Kievan Rus' to the religious and cultural world of Byzantium."},{"id":"EXP77-1474","nodeId":"EXP77-1474","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q057","subject":"Henry IV's journey to Canossa belongs to which dispute?","value":"Investiture Controversy","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_to_Canossa"}],"explanation74":"The conflict concerned relations between imperial and papal authority, especially the appointment of bishops."},{"id":"EXP77-1475","nodeId":"EXP77-1475","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"The Treaty of Campo Formio followed Napoleon's campaign in which region?","value":"Italy","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"place geography","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Campo_Formio"}],"explanation74":"The 1797 treaty with Austria followed Napoleon's successful Italian campaign."},{"id":"EXP77-1476","nodeId":"EXP77-1476","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Charles Martel's victory near Tours was fought against forces of which caliphate?","value":"Umayyad","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tours"}],"explanation74":"The battle of 732 checked an Umayyad expedition into Frankish territory."},{"id":"EXP77-1477","nodeId":"EXP77-1477","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q122","subject":"Napoleon's victories at Jena and Auerstedt were won against which power?","value":"Prussia","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt"}],"explanation74":"The twin battles of October 1806 shattered the Prussian army."},{"id":"EXP77-1478","nodeId":"EXP77-1478","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"NATO founded","value":"1949","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://nato.int/en/about-us/organization/founding-treaty"}],"explanation74":"NATO founded: 1949. The North Atlantic Treaty was signed on 4 April; West Germany joined only in 1955."},{"id":"EXP77-1479","nodeId":"EXP77-1479","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Rome's victory at Pydna ended the power of which kingdom?","value":"Antigonid Macedonia","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pydna"}],"explanation74":"The Roman victory of 168 BCE defeated King Perseus and ended the Antigonid monarchy in Macedonia."},{"id":"EXP77-1480","nodeId":"EXP77-1480","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"The Edict of Thessalonica is associated with imperial support for which religion?","value":"Nicene Christianity","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Thessalonica"}],"explanation74":"The edict of 380 endorsed the Nicene form of Christianity within the Roman Empire."},{"id":"EXP77-1481","nodeId":"EXP77-1481","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"The Jacquerie was a fourteenth-century peasant uprising in which country?","value":"France","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"place geography","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacquerie"}],"explanation74":"The Jacquerie broke out in northern France in 1358, amid the disruption of the Hundred Years' War."},{"id":"EXP77-1482","nodeId":"EXP77-1482","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"The early Visigothic kingdom in Aquitaine was centred on which city?","value":"Toulouse","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"place geography","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visigothic_Kingdom"}],"explanation74":"After the settlement of 418, Toulouse became the centre of Visigothic power in southern Gaul; Toledo belongs to a later phase."},{"id":"EXP77-1483","nodeId":"EXP77-1483","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q308","subject":"Luther's Ninety-five Theses","value":"1517","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninety-five_Theses"}],"explanation74":"Luther's Ninety-five Theses: 1517. Conventional opening of the Protestant Reformation."},{"id":"EXP77-1484","nodeId":"EXP77-1484","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q490","subject":"Galileo's 1633 trial centred on his support for which astronomical model?","value":"Heliocentrism","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Ancient","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_affair"}],"explanation74":"Galileo defended the motion of Earth around the Sun, in conflict with the Church's restrictions on Copernican teaching."},{"id":"EXP77-1485","nodeId":"EXP77-1485","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q696","subject":"Henry VIII marries Anne Boleyn","value":"1533","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Boleyn"}],"explanation74":"Henry VIII marries Anne Boleyn: 1533. Marriage preceded the 1534 Act of Supremacy."},{"id":"EXP77-1486","nodeId":"EXP77-1486","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q667","subject":"Imperial coronation of Charlemagne","value":"800","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne"}],"explanation74":"Imperial coronation of Charlemagne: 800. 25 December; Pope Leo III."},{"id":"EXP77-1487","nodeId":"EXP77-1487","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Castillon","value":"1453","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Castillon"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Castillon: 1453. Conventional end of the Hundred Years' War."},{"id":"EXP77-1488","nodeId":"EXP77-1488","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Pepin the Short becomes king","value":"751","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin_the_Short"}],"explanation74":"Pepin the Short becomes king: 751. Beginning of Carolingian royal rule."},{"id":"EXP77-1489","nodeId":"EXP77-1489","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q149","subject":"On the Origin of Species published","value":"1859","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_the_Origin_of_Species"}],"explanation74":"On the Origin of Species published: 1859. Darwin explained evolution by natural selection; distinguish scientific theory from later political misuse."},{"id":"EXP77-1490","nodeId":"EXP77-1490","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Kosovo","value":"1389","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Kosovo"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Kosovo: 1389. Medieval Serbian and Ottoman forces; losses on both sides."},{"id":"EXP77-1491","nodeId":"EXP77-1491","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Diet of Worms","value":"1521","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diet_of_Worms"}],"explanation74":"Diet of Worms: 1521. Luther before Charles V."},{"id":"EXP77-1492","nodeId":"EXP77-1492","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Nicopolis","value":"1396","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Nicopolis"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Nicopolis: 1396. Ottoman victory over a crusading coalition."},{"id":"EXP77-1493","nodeId":"EXP77-1493","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q212","subject":"Ivan IV crowned tsar","value":"1547","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_the_Terrible"}],"explanation74":"Ivan IV crowned tsar: 1547. Tsardom of Russia."},{"id":"EXP77-1494","nodeId":"EXP77-1494","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q227","subject":"Papal return to Rome","value":"1377","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregory_XI"}],"explanation74":"Papal return to Rome: 1377. Gregory XI leaves Avignon."},{"id":"EXP77-1495","nodeId":"EXP77-1495","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Traditional foundation of Rome","value":"753 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Founding_of_Rome"}],"explanation74":"Traditional foundation of Rome: 753 BCE. Roman tradition; archaeological settlement predates this date."},{"id":"EXP77-1496","nodeId":"EXP77-1496","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Gunpowder Plot","value":"1605","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder_Plot"}],"explanation74":"Gunpowder Plot: 1605. Failed plot against James I and Parliament in England."},{"id":"EXP77-1497","nodeId":"EXP77-1497","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q493","subject":"Battle of the Milvian Bridge","value":"312","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Milvian_Bridge"}],"explanation74":"Battle of the Milvian Bridge: 312. Constantine defeats Maxentius."},{"id":"EXP77-1498","nodeId":"EXP77-1498","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Saladin becomes vizier in Egypt","value":"1169","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin"}],"explanation74":"Saladin becomes vizier in Egypt: 1169. Ayyubid rule begins in 1171."},{"id":"EXP77-1499","nodeId":"EXP77-1499","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Karlowitz","value":"1699","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Karlowitz"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Karlowitz: 1699. Ottoman territorial losses in central Europe."},{"id":"EXP77-1500","nodeId":"EXP77-1500","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Gregorian calendar introduced","value":"1582","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar"}],"explanation74":"Gregorian calendar introduced: 1582. Initial adoption varied between countries."},{"id":"EXP77-1501","nodeId":"EXP77-1501","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"Act of Abjuration","value":"1581","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Act_of_Abjuration"}],"explanation74":"Act of Abjuration: 1581. Dutch provinces reject Philip II's rule."},{"id":"EXP77-1502","nodeId":"EXP77-1502","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q126","subject":"Fall of Constantinople","value":"1453","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Medieval","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_Constantinople"}],"explanation74":"Fall of Constantinople: 1453. Mehmed II conquers the Byzantine capital."},{"id":"EXP77-1503","nodeId":"EXP77-1503","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q109","subject":"War of Jenkins' Ear begins","value":"1739","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_Jenkins'_Ear"}],"explanation74":"War of Jenkins' Ear begins: 1739. Britain and Spain."},{"id":"EXP77-1504","nodeId":"EXP77-1504","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Outrage of Anagni","value":"1303","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outrage_of_Anagni"}],"explanation74":"Outrage of Anagni: 1303. Boniface VIII and agents of Philip IV."},{"id":"EXP77-1505","nodeId":"EXP77-1505","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Bosworth","value":"1485","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Bosworth_Field"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Bosworth: 1485. Henry VII defeats Richard III; Tudor dynasty."},{"id":"EXP77-1506","nodeId":"EXP77-1506","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q121","subject":"French invasion of Italy","value":"1494","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_War_of_1494%E2%80%931495"}],"explanation74":"French invasion of Italy: 1494. Charles VIII; Medici expelled from Florence."},{"id":"EXP77-1507","nodeId":"EXP77-1507","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Napoleon crowned emperor","value":"1804","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_Napoleon"}],"explanation74":"Napoleon crowned emperor: 1804. First French Empire."},{"id":"EXP77-1508","nodeId":"EXP77-1508","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"German Democratic Republic established","value":"1949","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Germany"}],"explanation74":"German Democratic Republic established: 1949. The East German state was proclaimed in October in the Soviet occupation zone."},{"id":"EXP77-1509","nodeId":"EXP77-1509","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q703","subject":"Newcomen atmospheric engine","value":"1712","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newcomen_atmospheric_engine"}],"explanation74":"Newcomen atmospheric engine: 1712. First successful commercial engine conventionally dated 1712."},{"id":"EXP77-1510","nodeId":"EXP77-1510","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"US Constitution signed","value":"1787","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Constitution"}],"explanation74":"US Constitution signed: 1787. Constitutional Convention."},{"id":"EXP77-1511","nodeId":"EXP77-1511","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"Teutonic Order founded","value":"1190","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teutonic_Order"}],"explanation74":"Teutonic Order founded: 1190. Hospital fraternity at Acre; military order from 1198."},{"id":"EXP77-1512","nodeId":"EXP77-1512","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Columbus reaches the Caribbean","value":"1492","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyages_of_Christopher_Columbus"}],"explanation74":"Columbus reaches the Caribbean: 1492. First transatlantic expedition reaches Caribbean islands."},{"id":"EXP77-1513","nodeId":"EXP77-1513","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Edict of Nantes","value":"1598","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Nantes"}],"explanation74":"Edict of Nantes: 1598. Religious settlement under Henry IV."},{"id":"EXP77-1514","nodeId":"EXP77-1514","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q494","subject":"Peace of Cateau-Cambrésis","value":"1559","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Cateau-Cambr%C3%A9sis"}],"explanation74":"Peace of Cateau-Cambrésis: 1559. Ends the principal phase of the Italian Wars."},{"id":"EXP77-1515","nodeId":"EXP77-1515","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Cabral reaches Brazil","value":"1500","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_%C3%81lvares_Cabral"}],"explanation74":"Cabral reaches Brazil: 1500. Portuguese Atlantic expedition."},{"id":"EXP77-1516","nodeId":"EXP77-1516","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Hijra","value":"622","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijrah"}],"explanation74":"Hijra: 622. Muhammad's migration to Medina; Islamic calendar epoch."},{"id":"EXP77-1517","nodeId":"EXP77-1517","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q602","subject":"Decian persecution","value":"250","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decian_persecution"}],"explanation74":"Decian persecution: 250. Empire-wide sacrifice requirement under Decius."},{"id":"EXP77-1518","nodeId":"EXP77-1518","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q308","subject":"Pugachev's Rebellion begins","value":"1773","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pugachev's_Rebellion"}],"explanation74":"Pugachev's Rebellion begins: 1773. Major uprising in the Russian Empire, suppressed by 1775."},{"id":"EXP77-1519","nodeId":"EXP77-1519","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"Navigation Act","value":"1651","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navigation_Acts"}],"explanation74":"Navigation Act: 1651. Maritime trade restrictions."},{"id":"EXP77-1520","nodeId":"EXP77-1520","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"École Polytechnique founded","value":"1794","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89cole_Polytechnique"}],"explanation74":"École Polytechnique founded: 1794. Originally École centrale des travaux publics."},{"id":"EXP77-1521","nodeId":"EXP77-1521","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q335","subject":"Assassination of Julius Caesar","value":"44 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Julius_Caesar"}],"explanation74":"Assassination of Julius Caesar: 44 BCE. 15 March."},{"id":"EXP77-1522","nodeId":"EXP77-1522","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Mayflower voyage","value":"1620","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayflower"}],"explanation74":"Mayflower voyage: 1620. Pilgrims and Plymouth colony."},{"id":"EXP77-1523","nodeId":"EXP77-1523","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q515","subject":"French First Republic proclaimed","value":"1792","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_First_Republic"}],"explanation74":"French First Republic proclaimed: 1792. Monarchy abolished in September."},{"id":"EXP77-1524","nodeId":"EXP77-1524","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q451","subject":"League of Cambrai","value":"1508","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/League_of_Cambrai"}],"explanation74":"League of Cambrai: 1508. Alliance initially directed against Venice."},{"id":"EXP77-1525","nodeId":"EXP77-1525","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Austerlitz","value":"1805","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Austerlitz"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Austerlitz: 1805. French victory over Russia and Austria."},{"id":"EXP77-1526","nodeId":"EXP77-1526","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q495","subject":"Joseph Bonaparte placed on the Spanish throne","value":"1808","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Bonaparte"}],"explanation74":"Joseph Bonaparte placed on the Spanish throne: 1808. Peninsular War context."},{"id":"EXP77-1527","nodeId":"EXP77-1527","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q500","subject":"Byzantine recovery of Constantinople","value":"1261","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Ancient","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reconquest_of_Constantinople"}],"explanation74":"Byzantine recovery of Constantinople: 1261. Michael VIII Palaiologos."},{"id":"EXP77-1528","nodeId":"EXP77-1528","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Tertry","value":"687","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tertry"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Tertry: 687. Pepin of Herstal consolidates power."},{"id":"EXP77-1529","nodeId":"EXP77-1529","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q126","subject":"Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire","value":"1806","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Medieval","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dissolution_of_the_Holy_Roman_Empire"}],"explanation74":"Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire: 1806. Francis II abdicates the imperial title."},{"id":"EXP77-1530","nodeId":"EXP77-1530","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Waterloo","value":"1815","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Waterloo"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Waterloo: 1815. 18 June; Napoleon's final defeat."},{"id":"EXP77-1531","nodeId":"EXP77-1531","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Magna Carta","value":"1215","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magna_Carta"}],"explanation74":"Magna Carta: 1215. King John and the barons."},{"id":"EXP77-1532","nodeId":"EXP77-1532","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Valois dynasty begins","value":"1328","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_VI_of_France"}],"explanation74":"Valois dynasty begins: 1328. Philip VI succeeds the direct Capetian line."},{"id":"EXP77-1533","nodeId":"EXP77-1533","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle","value":"1748","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Aix-la-Chapelle_(1748)"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle: 1748. Ends the Austrian Succession war."},{"id":"EXP77-1534","nodeId":"EXP77-1534","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q770","subject":"Acts of Union","value":"1707","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Late 20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acts_of_Union_1707"}],"explanation74":"Acts of Union: 1707. Kingdom of Great Britain formed."},{"id":"EXP77-1535","nodeId":"EXP77-1535","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q456","subject":"Battle of Trafalgar","value":"1805","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Trafalgar"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Trafalgar: 1805. Nelson's naval victory."},{"id":"EXP77-1536","nodeId":"EXP77-1536","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q446","subject":"Tennis Court Oath","value":"1789","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis_Court_Oath"}],"explanation74":"Tennis Court Oath: 1789. 20 June; French National Assembly."},{"id":"EXP77-1537","nodeId":"EXP77-1537","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Italian republic referendum","value":"1946","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.quirinale.it/it/pagine/2-giugno-1946-2-giugno-2016"}],"explanation74":"Italian republic referendum: 1946. Voting on 2–3 June chose a republic; Enrico De Nicola became provisional head of state later that month."},{"id":"EXP77-1538","nodeId":"EXP77-1538","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"Jamestown founded","value":"1607","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamestown,_Virginia"}],"explanation74":"Jamestown founded: 1607. English settlement in Virginia."},{"id":"EXP77-1539","nodeId":"EXP77-1539","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Paris","value":"1763","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1763)"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Paris: 1763. Britain, France and Spain."},{"id":"EXP77-1540","nodeId":"EXP77-1540","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Wagram","value":"1809","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wagram"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Wagram: 1809. French victory over Austria."},{"id":"EXP77-1541","nodeId":"EXP77-1541","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q621","subject":"Death of Alexander the Great","value":"323 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Ancient","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_the_Great"}],"explanation74":"Death of Alexander the Great: 323 BCE. The successor kingdoms emerge after his death."},{"id":"EXP77-1542","nodeId":"EXP77-1542","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Sack of Rome","value":"1527","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sack_of_Rome_(1527)"}],"explanation74":"Sack of Rome: 1527. Imperial troops sack the city."},{"id":"EXP77-1543","nodeId":"EXP77-1543","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Das Kapital, volume I published","value":"1867","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Das_Kapital"}],"explanation74":"Das Kapital, volume I published: 1867. Marx's critique of capitalist production; distinguish from the 1848 Manifesto."},{"id":"EXP77-1544","nodeId":"EXP77-1544","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Brétigny","value":"1360","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Br%C3%A9tigny"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Brétigny: 1360. Also associated with the settlement at Calais."},{"id":"EXP77-1545","nodeId":"EXP77-1545","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Kingdom of Prussia proclaimed","value":"1701","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Prussia"}],"explanation74":"Kingdom of Prussia proclaimed: 1701. Frederick I crowned king in Prussia."},{"id":"EXP77-1546","nodeId":"EXP77-1546","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"German Confederation founded","value":"1815","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Confederation"}],"explanation74":"German Confederation founded: 1815. Created at Vienna."},{"id":"EXP77-1547","nodeId":"EXP77-1547","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Ryswick","value":"1697","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Ryswick"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Ryswick: 1697. Ends the Nine Years' War."},{"id":"EXP77-1548","nodeId":"EXP77-1548","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Verdun","value":"843","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Verdun"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Verdun: 843. Carolingian empire partitioned into three kingdoms."},{"id":"EXP77-1549","nodeId":"EXP77-1549","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q189","subject":"Tasman's first Pacific voyage","value":"1642","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abel_Tasman"}],"explanation74":"Tasman's first Pacific voyage: 1642. European encounter with Tasmania and New Zealand; not the first human settlement of either."},{"id":"EXP77-1550","nodeId":"EXP77-1550","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Lechfeld","value":"955","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lechfeld"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Lechfeld: 955. Otto I defeats the Magyars."},{"id":"EXP77-1551","nodeId":"EXP77-1551","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Leipzig","value":"1813","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Leipzig"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Leipzig: 1813. Battle of the Nations."},{"id":"EXP77-1552","nodeId":"EXP77-1552","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Fundamental Orders of Connecticut","value":"1639","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamental_Orders_of_Connecticut"}],"explanation74":"Fundamental Orders of Connecticut: 1639. Colonial constitutional document."},{"id":"EXP77-1553","nodeId":"EXP77-1553","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Zama","value":"202 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Zama"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Zama: 202 BCE. Scipio defeats Hannibal."},{"id":"EXP77-1554","nodeId":"EXP77-1554","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q642","subject":"Execution of Louis XVI","value":"1793","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Execution_of_Louis_XVI"}],"explanation74":"Execution of Louis XVI: 1793. 21 January."},{"id":"EXP77-1555","nodeId":"EXP77-1555","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Bank of Amsterdam founded","value":"1609","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_Amsterdam"}],"explanation74":"Bank of Amsterdam founded: 1609. Amsterdam Wisselbank."},{"id":"EXP77-1556","nodeId":"EXP77-1556","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q308","subject":"Toscanelli's Atlantic proposal","value":"1474","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paolo_dal_Pozzo_Toscanelli"}],"explanation74":"Toscanelli's Atlantic proposal: 1474. Letter and map proposing a westward route to Asia; the original map does not survive."},{"id":"EXP77-1557","nodeId":"EXP77-1557","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Agincourt","value":"1415","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Agincourt"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Agincourt: 1415. Henry V defeats a French army."},{"id":"EXP77-1558","nodeId":"EXP77-1558","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q308","subject":"Watt's separate-condenser patent","value":"1769","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Watt"}],"explanation74":"Watt's separate-condenser patent: 1769. Patent milestone; development began earlier."},{"id":"EXP77-1559","nodeId":"EXP77-1559","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q148","subject":"Ottomans establish a foothold at Gallipoli","value":"1354","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_Gallipoli"}],"explanation74":"Ottomans establish a foothold at Gallipoli: 1354. A key stage in expansion into Europe."},{"id":"EXP77-1560","nodeId":"EXP77-1560","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q690","subject":"Third Partition of Poland","value":"1795","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early 20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Partition_of_Poland"}],"explanation74":"Third Partition of Poland: 1795. Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth disappears from the map."},{"id":"EXP77-1561","nodeId":"EXP77-1561","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q607","subject":"Vasco da Gama reaches India","value":"1498","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasco_da_Gama"}],"explanation74":"Vasco da Gama reaches India: 1498. Arrival at Calicut."},{"id":"EXP77-1562","nodeId":"EXP77-1562","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Federal Republic of Germany established","value":"1949","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Germany"}],"explanation74":"Federal Republic of Germany established: 1949. The Basic Law took effect in May; Adenauer became chancellor in September."},{"id":"EXP77-1563","nodeId":"EXP77-1563","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q494","subject":"Peace of Westphalia","value":"1648","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Westphalia"}],"explanation74":"Peace of Westphalia: 1648. Treaties ending the Thirty Years' War."},{"id":"EXP77-1564","nodeId":"EXP77-1564","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Charles I begins Personal Rule","value":"1629","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_Rule"}],"explanation74":"Charles I begins Personal Rule: 1629. Period without Parliament, ending 1640."},{"id":"EXP77-1565","nodeId":"EXP77-1565","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Varna","value":"1444","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Varna"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Varna: 1444. Ottoman victory."},{"id":"EXP77-1566","nodeId":"EXP77-1566","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q103","subject":"Rosetta Stone discovered by French soldiers","value":"1799","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosetta_Stone"}],"explanation74":"Rosetta Stone discovered by French soldiers: 1799. Found during the Egyptian expedition; Champollion's decipherment announcement followed in 1822."},{"id":"EXP77-1567","nodeId":"EXP77-1567","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Great Fire of Rome","value":"64","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Fire_of_Rome"}],"explanation74":"Great Fire of Rome: 64. Nero's reign; persecution followed."},{"id":"EXP77-1568","nodeId":"EXP77-1568","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q754","subject":"Ostrogothic rule in Italy begins","value":"493","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early 20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrogothic_Kingdom"}],"explanation74":"Ostrogothic rule in Italy begins: 493. Theoderic defeats Odoacer."},{"id":"EXP77-1569","nodeId":"EXP77-1569","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Pharsalus","value":"48 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pharsalus"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Pharsalus: 48 BCE. Caesar defeats Pompey."},{"id":"EXP77-1570","nodeId":"EXP77-1570","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"Québec founded","value":"1608","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Quebec_City"}],"explanation74":"Québec founded: 1608. Samuel de Champlain."},{"id":"EXP77-1571","nodeId":"EXP77-1571","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q057","subject":"Henry IV converts to Catholicism","value":"1593","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_IV_of_France"}],"explanation74":"Henry IV converts to Catholicism: 1593. Associated with the traditional saying about Paris and a Mass."},{"id":"EXP77-1572","nodeId":"EXP77-1572","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q057","subject":"Court moves to Versailles","value":"1682","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palace_of_Versailles"}],"explanation74":"Court moves to Versailles: 1682. Versailles becomes the principal royal residence."},{"id":"EXP77-1573","nodeId":"EXP77-1573","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q409","subject":"First secession of the plebs","value":"494 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secessio_plebis"}],"explanation74":"First secession of the plebs: 494 BCE. Traditionally to the Sacred Mount; some accounts associate the Aventine."},{"id":"EXP77-1574","nodeId":"EXP77-1574","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Charlemagne conquers the Lombard kingdom","value":"774","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Pavia_(773%E2%80%93774)"}],"explanation74":"Charlemagne conquers the Lombard kingdom: 774. Pavia falls to the Franks."},{"id":"EXP77-1575","nodeId":"EXP77-1575","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Warsaw Pact formed","value":"1955","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.nato.int/cps/en/natohq/declassified_138294.htm"}],"explanation74":"Warsaw Pact formed: 1955. Formed after West Germany joined NATO; the two alliances structured much of Cold War Europe."},{"id":"EXP77-1576","nodeId":"EXP77-1576","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q450","subject":"Eruption of Vesuvius","value":"79","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eruption_of_Mount_Vesuvius_in_79_AD"}],"explanation74":"Eruption of Vesuvius: 79. Pompeii and Herculaneum."},{"id":"EXP77-1577","nodeId":"EXP77-1577","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q103","subject":"Revocation of the Edict of Nantes","value":"1685","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Fontainebleau"}],"explanation74":"Revocation of the Edict of Nantes: 1685. Louis XIV ends the earlier religious settlement."},{"id":"EXP77-1578","nodeId":"EXP77-1578","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Benevento","value":"1266","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Benevento"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Benevento: 1266. Charles of Anjou defeats Manfred of Sicily; distinct from the later Sicilian Vespers."},{"id":"EXP77-1579","nodeId":"EXP77-1579","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q456","subject":"Battle of Hastings and Norman conquest","value":"1066","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hastings"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Hastings and Norman conquest: 1066. William defeats Harold II."},{"id":"EXP77-1580","nodeId":"EXP77-1580","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Catholic Emancipation","value":"1829","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Catholic_Relief_Act_1829"}],"explanation74":"Catholic Emancipation: 1829. United Kingdom."},{"id":"EXP77-1581","nodeId":"EXP77-1581","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q453","subject":"St Bartholomew's Day massacre","value":"1572","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Bartholomew's_Day_massacre"}],"explanation74":"St Bartholomew's Day massacre: 1572. French Wars of Religion."},{"id":"EXP77-1582","nodeId":"EXP77-1582","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q109","subject":"Greek War of Independence begins","value":"1821","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_War_of_Independence"}],"explanation74":"Greek War of Independence begins: 1821. Ottoman rule challenged."},{"id":"EXP77-1583","nodeId":"EXP77-1583","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Treaty of Paris recognises US independence","value":"1783","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1783)"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Paris recognises US independence: 1783. Ends the Anglo-American war."},{"id":"EXP77-1584","nodeId":"EXP77-1584","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"Restoration of the English monarchy","value":"1660","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_Restoration"}],"explanation74":"Restoration of the English monarchy: 1660. Charles II returns."},{"id":"EXP77-1585","nodeId":"EXP77-1585","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Napoleon's first abdication","value":"1814","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Fontainebleau_(1814)"}],"explanation74":"Napoleon's first abdication: 1814. Exile to Elba."},{"id":"EXP77-1586","nodeId":"EXP77-1586","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q078","subject":"Augustan settlement","value":"27 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus"}],"explanation74":"Augustan settlement: 27 BCE. Octavian receives the title Augustus."},{"id":"EXP77-1587","nodeId":"EXP77-1587","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q057","subject":"Lombards enter Italy","value":"568","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lombard_Kingdom"}],"explanation74":"Lombards enter Italy: 568. Alboin's invasion."},{"id":"EXP77-1588","nodeId":"EXP77-1588","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q223","subject":"Death of Cleopatra VII","value":"30 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra"}],"explanation74":"Death of Cleopatra VII: 30 BCE. Egypt becomes a Roman province."},{"id":"EXP77-1589","nodeId":"EXP77-1589","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Traditional foundation of Carthage","value":"814 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthage"}],"explanation74":"Traditional foundation of Carthage: 814 BCE. Traditional date, not a securely dated founding event."},{"id":"EXP77-1590","nodeId":"EXP77-1590","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q684","subject":"Brandenburg–Prussia personal union","value":"1618","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandenburg-Prussia"}],"explanation74":"Brandenburg–Prussia personal union: 1618. Hohenzollern dynastic union."},{"id":"EXP77-1591","nodeId":"EXP77-1591","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q197","subject":"Delian League founded","value":"478 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delian_League"}],"explanation74":"Delian League founded: 478 BCE. Athenian-led alliance."},{"id":"EXP77-1592","nodeId":"EXP77-1592","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q223","subject":"Lorenzo de' Medici assumes leadership","value":"1469","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorenzo_de'_Medici"}],"explanation74":"Lorenzo de' Medici assumes leadership: 1469. Florentine political leadership after Piero's death."},{"id":"EXP77-1593","nodeId":"EXP77-1593","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Kingdom of Sicily established","value":"1130","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Sicily"}],"explanation74":"Kingdom of Sicily established: 1130. Roger II crowned king."},{"id":"EXP77-1594","nodeId":"EXP77-1594","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Lepanto","value":"1571","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lepanto"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Lepanto: 1571. Holy League naval victory over the Ottomans."},{"id":"EXP77-1595","nodeId":"EXP77-1595","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Continental System proclaimed","value":"1806","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continental_System"}],"explanation74":"Continental System proclaimed: 1806. Berlin Decree."},{"id":"EXP77-1596","nodeId":"EXP77-1596","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Abdication of Charles V","value":"1556","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_V,_Holy_Roman_Emperor"}],"explanation74":"Abdication of Charles V: 1556. Habsburg territories divided between family branches."},{"id":"EXP77-1597","nodeId":"EXP77-1597","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Blenheim","value":"1704","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Blenheim"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Blenheim: 1704. Grand Alliance victory."},{"id":"EXP77-1598","nodeId":"EXP77-1598","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q230","subject":"Florence dome competition","value":"1418","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florence_Cathedral"}],"explanation74":"Florence dome competition: 1418. Design competition precedes Brunelleschi's construction campaign beginning in 1420."},{"id":"EXP77-1599","nodeId":"EXP77-1599","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Treaties of Rome signed","value":"1957","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.europarl.europa.eu/about-parliament/en/in-the-past/the-parliament-and-the-treaties/treaty-of-rome"}],"explanation74":"Treaties of Rome signed: 1957. Signed on 25 March; the EEC and Euratom treaties entered into force on 1 January 1958."},{"id":"EXP77-1600","nodeId":"EXP77-1600","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q494","subject":"Peace of Asti","value":"1615","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Asti"}],"explanation74":"Peace of Asti: 1615. Settlement in the War of the Montferrat Succession."},{"id":"EXP77-1601","nodeId":"EXP77-1601","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Romanov dynasty begins","value":"1613","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_of_Russia"}],"explanation74":"Romanov dynasty begins: 1613. Michael I elected tsar."},{"id":"EXP77-1602","nodeId":"EXP77-1602","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q517","subject":"Execution of Jan Hus","value":"1415","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Hus"}],"explanation74":"Execution of Jan Hus: 1415. Burned at Constance."},{"id":"EXP77-1603","nodeId":"EXP77-1603","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q456","subject":"Revolutions in Spain and Naples","value":"1820","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolutions_during_the_1820s"}],"explanation74":"Revolutions in Spain and Naples: 1820. Constitutional movements."},{"id":"EXP77-1604","nodeId":"EXP77-1604","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q223","subject":"Death of Muhammad","value":"632","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad"}],"explanation74":"Death of Muhammad: 632. Beginning of the caliphal succession."},{"id":"EXP77-1605","nodeId":"EXP77-1605","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"Declaration of the Rights of Man and Citizen","value":"1789","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Declaration_of_the_Rights_of_Man_and_of_the_Citizen"}],"explanation74":"Declaration of the Rights of Man and Citizen: 1789. 26 August."},{"id":"EXP77-1606","nodeId":"EXP77-1606","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Edict of Milan","value":"313","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Milan"}],"explanation74":"Edict of Milan: 313. Constantine and Licinius agree religious toleration."},{"id":"EXP77-1607","nodeId":"EXP77-1607","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q121","subject":"The Communist Manifesto published","value":"1848","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Communist_Manifesto"}],"explanation74":"The Communist Manifesto published: 1848. Marx and Engels analysed class conflict and capitalism; publication coincided with, but did not cause all, the revolutions."},{"id":"EXP77-1608","nodeId":"EXP77-1608","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Hugh Capet becomes king","value":"987","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Capet"}],"explanation74":"Hugh Capet becomes king: 987. Beginning of the Capetian dynasty."},{"id":"EXP77-1609","nodeId":"EXP77-1609","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q079","subject":"Æthelstan unites England","value":"927","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86thelstan"}],"explanation74":"Æthelstan unites England: 927. Often regarded as the first king of all England."},{"id":"EXP77-1610","nodeId":"EXP77-1610","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Society of Jesus approved","value":"1540","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Society_of_Jesus"}],"explanation74":"Society of Jesus approved: 1540. Papal approval under Paul III."},{"id":"EXP77-1611","nodeId":"EXP77-1611","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Execution of Charles I","value":"1649","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Execution_of_Charles_I"}],"explanation74":"Execution of Charles I: 1649. English monarchy abolished temporarily."},{"id":"EXP77-1612","nodeId":"EXP77-1612","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Treaty of Meerssen","value":"870","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Meerssen"}],"explanation74":"Treaty of Meerssen: 870. Division of Lothair II's kingdom between East and West Francia."},{"id":"EXP77-1613","nodeId":"EXP77-1613","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Champollion announces hieroglyphic decipherment","value":"1822","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois_Champollion"}],"explanation74":"Champollion announces hieroglyphic decipherment: 1822. Lettre à M. Dacier; a major milestone, not the initial discovery of the Rosetta Stone."},{"id":"EXP77-1614","nodeId":"EXP77-1614","anchor":"ALPHA-B006-Q642","subject":"July Revolution in France","value":"1830","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_Revolution"}],"explanation74":"July Revolution in France: 1830. Charles X overthrown; Louis-Philippe succeeds."},{"id":"EXP77-1615","nodeId":"EXP77-1615","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q515","subject":"Dias rounds southern Africa","value":"1488","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartolomeu_Dias"}],"explanation74":"Dias rounds southern Africa: 1488. Cape of Good Hope voyage."},{"id":"EXP77-1616","nodeId":"EXP77-1616","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Louisiana Purchase","value":"1803","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_Purchase"}],"explanation74":"Louisiana Purchase: 1803. United States acquisition from France."},{"id":"EXP77-1617","nodeId":"EXP77-1617","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q060","subject":"Young Italy founded","value":"1831","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_Italy"}],"explanation74":"Young Italy founded: 1831. Giuseppe Mazzini's movement."},{"id":"EXP77-1618","nodeId":"EXP77-1618","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q189","subject":"Galileo's first ecclesiastical warning","value":"1616","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_affair"}],"explanation74":"Galileo's first ecclesiastical warning: 1616. Distinct from his trial in 1633."},{"id":"EXP77-1619","nodeId":"EXP77-1619","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q694","subject":"End of the Sasanian Empire","value":"651","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yazdegerd_III"}],"explanation74":"End of the Sasanian Empire: 651. Death of the last Sasanian ruler."},{"id":"EXP77-1620","nodeId":"EXP77-1620","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Louis XIV becomes king","value":"1643","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_XIV"}],"explanation74":"Louis XIV becomes king: 1643. Mazarin directs government during the minority."},{"id":"EXP77-1621","nodeId":"EXP77-1621","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q103","subject":"Confederation of the Rhine","value":"1806","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederation_of_the_Rhine"}],"explanation74":"Confederation of the Rhine: 1806. Formation precedes dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire."},{"id":"EXP77-1622","nodeId":"EXP77-1622","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q221","subject":"First Ottoman siege of Vienna","value":"1529","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Vienna_(1529)"}],"explanation74":"First Ottoman siege of Vienna: 1529. Suleiman's campaign."},{"id":"EXP77-1623","nodeId":"EXP77-1623","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q494","subject":"Peace of Augsburg","value":"1555","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Augsburg"}],"explanation74":"Peace of Augsburg: 1555. Settlement concerning Lutheran and Catholic imperial estates."},{"id":"EXP77-1624","nodeId":"EXP77-1624","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Napoleon invades Russia","value":"1812","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_invasion_of_Russia"}],"explanation74":"Napoleon invades Russia: 1812. Catastrophic retreat."},{"id":"EXP77-1625","nodeId":"EXP77-1625","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"English Bill of Rights","value":"1689","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_of_Rights_1689"}],"explanation74":"English Bill of Rights: 1689. Constitutional settlement."},{"id":"EXP77-1626","nodeId":"EXP77-1626","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q684","subject":"Kalmar Union","value":"1397","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"19th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union"}],"explanation74":"Kalmar Union: 1397. Denmark, Norway and Sweden."},{"id":"EXP77-1627","nodeId":"EXP77-1627","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q057","subject":"Russian court moves to Saint Petersburg","value":"1712","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Petersburg"}],"explanation74":"Russian court moves to Saint Petersburg: 1712. Capital transfer traditionally dated 1712."},{"id":"EXP77-1628","nodeId":"EXP77-1628","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Second Partition of Poland","value":"1793","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Partition_of_Poland"}],"explanation74":"Second Partition of Poland: 1793. Russia and Prussia."},{"id":"EXP77-1629","nodeId":"EXP77-1629","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q281","subject":"Execution of Savonarola","value":"1498","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girolamo_Savonarola"}],"explanation74":"Execution of Savonarola: 1498. Florence."},{"id":"EXP77-1630","nodeId":"EXP77-1630","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q211","subject":"Kingdom of Italy proclaimed","value":"1861","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.quirinale.it/it/pagine/simboli-repubblica-tricolore"}],"explanation74":"Kingdom of Italy proclaimed: 1861. Proclaimed on 17 March under Victor Emmanuel II; Rome and Venice were not yet included."},{"id":"EXP77-1631","nodeId":"EXP77-1631","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Napoleon becomes First Consul for life","value":"1802","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon"}],"explanation74":"Napoleon becomes First Consul for life: 1802. Life consulate."},{"id":"EXP77-1632","nodeId":"EXP77-1632","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Ankara","value":"1402","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ankara"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Ankara: 1402. Timur defeats Bayezid I."},{"id":"EXP77-1633","nodeId":"EXP77-1633","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Traditional foundation of Bologna University","value":"1088","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Bologna"}],"explanation74":"Traditional foundation of Bologna University: 1088. Conventional institutional foundation date."},{"id":"EXP77-1634","nodeId":"EXP77-1634","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q279","subject":"Louis XIV begins personal rule","value":"1661","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_XIV"}],"explanation74":"Louis XIV begins personal rule: 1661. After Mazarin's death."},{"id":"EXP77-1635","nodeId":"EXP77-1635","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q503","subject":"Duchy of Normandy established","value":"911","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"20th century","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Saint-Clair-sur-Epte"}],"explanation74":"Duchy of Normandy established: 911. Settlement associated with Rollo."},{"id":"EXP77-1636","nodeId":"EXP77-1636","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q103","subject":"Constitutio Antoniniana","value":"212","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutio_Antoniniana"}],"explanation74":"Constitutio Antoniniana: 212. Caracalla extends Roman citizenship to most free inhabitants."},{"id":"EXP77-1637","nodeId":"EXP77-1637","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q753","subject":"Act of Supremacy","value":"1534","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acts_of_Supremacy"}],"explanation74":"Act of Supremacy: 1534. English royal supremacy over the church."},{"id":"EXP77-1638","nodeId":"EXP77-1638","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Dedication of Constantinople","value":"330","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantinople"}],"explanation74":"Dedication of Constantinople: 330. Constantine's imperial capital."},{"id":"EXP77-1639","nodeId":"EXP77-1639","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Grunwald / Tannenberg","value":"1410","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Grunwald"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Grunwald / Tannenberg: 1410. Polish–Lithuanian victory over the Teutonic Order."},{"id":"EXP77-1640","nodeId":"EXP77-1640","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q023","subject":"Ayyubid dynasty in Egypt","value":"1171","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayyubid_dynasty"}],"explanation74":"Ayyubid dynasty in Egypt: 1171. Saladin ends Fatimid rule."},{"id":"EXP77-1641","nodeId":"EXP77-1641","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q317","subject":"Habeas Corpus Act","value":"1679","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habeas_Corpus_Act_1679"}],"explanation74":"Habeas Corpus Act: 1679. English legal protection against unlawful detention."},{"id":"EXP77-1642","nodeId":"EXP77-1642","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q095","subject":"Battle of Chaeronea","value":"338 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chaeronea_(338_BC)"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Chaeronea: 338 BCE. Philip II defeats the Greek coalition."},{"id":"EXP77-1643","nodeId":"EXP77-1643","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q266","subject":"Council of Clermont","value":"1095","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Clermont"}],"explanation74":"Council of Clermont: 1095. Urban II calls for the First Crusade."},{"id":"EXP77-1644","nodeId":"EXP77-1644","anchor":"ALPHA-B002-Q103","subject":"Great Fire of London","value":"1666","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Fire_of_London"}],"explanation74":"Great Fire of London: 1666. September fire; later rebuilding."},{"id":"EXP77-1645","nodeId":"EXP77-1645","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Carlsbad Decrees","value":"1819","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlsbad_Decrees"}],"explanation74":"Carlsbad Decrees: 1819. Repression of liberal and national movements."},{"id":"EXP77-1646","nodeId":"EXP77-1646","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Permanent division of imperial rule","value":"395","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire"}],"explanation74":"Permanent division of imperial rule: 395. After the death of Theodosius I."},{"id":"EXP77-1647","nodeId":"EXP77-1647","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q308","subject":"Fulton's commercial steamboat service","value":"1807","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Renaissance","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_River_Steamboat"}],"explanation74":"Fulton's commercial steamboat service: 1807. Hudson River service."},{"id":"EXP77-1648","nodeId":"EXP77-1648","anchor":"ALPHA-B003-Q223","subject":"Death of Lorenzo de' Medici","value":"1492","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorenzo_de'_Medici"}],"explanation74":"Death of Lorenzo de' Medici: 1492. A turning point in Florentine politics."},{"id":"EXP77-1649","nodeId":"EXP77-1649","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q292","subject":"Savoy acquires Sardinia","value":"1720","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Sardinia"}],"explanation74":"Savoy acquires Sardinia: 1720. Exchange of Sicily for Sardinia."},{"id":"EXP77-1650","nodeId":"EXP77-1650","anchor":"ALPHA-B008-Q755","subject":"Battle of Actium","value":"31 BCE","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Ancient","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Actium"}],"explanation74":"Battle of Actium: 31 BCE. Octavian defeats Antony and Cleopatra."},{"id":"EXP77-1651","nodeId":"EXP77-1651","anchor":"ALPHA-B007-Q492","subject":"Quadruple Alliance","value":"1815","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Medieval","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quadruple_Alliance_(1815)"}],"explanation74":"Quadruple Alliance: 1815. Britain, Austria, Prussia and Russia."},{"id":"EXP77-1652","nodeId":"EXP77-1652","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q446","subject":"French Revolution begins","value":"1789","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Revolution"}],"explanation74":"French Revolution begins: 1789. Estates-General; Tennis Court Oath; Bastille."},{"id":"EXP77-1653","nodeId":"EXP77-1653","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q040","subject":"Maastricht Treaty signed","value":"1992","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://european-union.europa.eu/principles-countries-history/history-eu/1990-99_en"}],"explanation74":"Maastricht Treaty signed: 1992. Signed on 7 February; the European Union formally began when the treaty entered into force in 1993."},{"id":"EXP77-1654","nodeId":"EXP77-1654","anchor":"ALPHA-B004-Q314","subject":"Tetrarchy established","value":"293","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Medieval","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrarchy"}],"explanation74":"Tetrarchy established: 293. Diocletian, Maximian, Galerius and Constantius Chlorus."},{"id":"EXP77-1655","nodeId":"EXP77-1655","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q013","subject":"Decembrist revolt","value":"1825","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decembrist_revolt"}],"explanation74":"Decembrist revolt: 1825. Russian uprising."},{"id":"EXP77-1656","nodeId":"EXP77-1656","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q454","subject":"Holy Alliance","value":"1815","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Alliance"}],"explanation74":"Holy Alliance: 1815. Russia, Austria and Prussia."},{"id":"EXP77-1657","nodeId":"EXP77-1657","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q452","subject":"Spanish Armada","value":"1588","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Armada"}],"explanation74":"Spanish Armada: 1588. Failed invasion campaign against England."},{"id":"EXP77-1658","nodeId":"EXP77-1658","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Petition of Right","value":"1628","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petition_of_Right"}],"explanation74":"Petition of Right: 1628. Parliament and Charles I."},{"id":"EXP77-1659","nodeId":"EXP77-1659","anchor":"ALPHA-B001-Q022","subject":"Italian Constitution enters into force","value":"1948","group":"history date","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"history date","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Italy"}],"explanation74":"Italian Constitution enters into force: 1948. Effective 1 January; the republican referendum was in 1946, not 1948."},{"id":"EXP77-1660","nodeId":"EXP77-1660","anchor":"ALPHA-B005-Q456","subject":"Henry IV of France","value":"Henry IV of France","group":"lifespan","major":"History & Politics","era":"Early modern","relation":"lifespan","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record","page":null,"verificationUrl